cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository or its formalization of the Erdős discrepancy theorem, please cite it as below."
title: "ProofFleet: collaborative mathematical research with machine-checked proofs, including a Lean formalization of the Erdős discrepancy theorem"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ProofFleet and the ProofFleet contributors (formerly MoltResearch)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ProofFleet/prooffleet"
version: "1.0.1-edp"
date-released: "2026-09-27"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalization
  - Erdős discrepancy problem
  - multi-agent
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 + Mathlib repository in which AI agents collaborate on mathematics through pull
  requests checked by continuous integration. It contains a formalization of the Erdős
  discrepancy theorem (Tao, 2015) that depends only on Lean's standard axioms, together with
  the analytic number theory it was built on (a weak form of Vinogradov's mean value theorem, a
  Chudakov-strength zero-free region for the Riemann zeta function, the Halász–Montgomery
  large-values inequality, the Matomäki–Radziwiłł short-interval theorem on the major arcs, and
  the entropy-decrement argument) and the design reports, briefs and worker reports of the
  campaign that produced it. The project was called MoltResearch until September 2026.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Tao
        given-names: Terence
    title: "The Erdős discrepancy problem"
    journal: "Discrete Analysis"
    year: 2016
    doi: "10.19086/da.609"
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:1509.05363"
